TODO, in order (bugs, then features, then optimization)

BUGS
 1. DONE synced lsp/tree-sitter-hylian (pushed cafdae0 to LinkNavi/tree-sitter-hylian; gitlink updated).
 2. DONE nested struct literals copy the value (tests/stdlib/nested_struct.hy).
 3. DONE (lexer-level GLT in compiler/lexer.l; tests/stdlib/generic_vs_compare.hy) was: grammar cannot tell an explicit generic call `max<int>(a, b)` from a comparison.
 4. DONE in compiler/parser.y (tests/stdlib/tuple_params.hy); tree-sitter/LSP grammars still lack it.

FEATURES
 5. DONE http/https no longer use map.hy (Response/Url structs, header arrays; a HashMap<V> can't
    be returned inside a struct, class values don't survive that); (T, Error?) used throughout.
    map.hy itself stays, with its test.
 6. PARTLY DONE http has real types (Response, Url). bytes Buffer is still a usize handle: a class
    can't escape the function that creates it (inflate returns its buffer), so it needs the
    language limitation lifted first.
 7. DONE (already current; rebuilt lsp, restored the missing tests/lsp fixture vendors/gfx/gfx.hyi, lsp_test.py all pass) was: rewrite lsp_analysis.c to match the current stdlib setup, class setup and zora.toml.
 8. DONE generic methods (`U map<U>(fn(T) -> U f)`, explicit or inferred type args): parser.y, mono.c
    (mono_instantiate_method), typecheck.c, tree-sitter grammar; tests/stdlib/generic_method.hy.
 9. DONE function pointers returning a struct by value (lower_indirect_call; tests/stdlib/fn_ptr_struct.hy).
10. DONE structs by value across the C ABI with nested structs, arrays, unions and padding
    (ast_c_layout + lower_marshal; tests/stdlib/ffi_nested.hy). Not: bool fields, float unions.
11. DONE .hyi accepts typed callbacks (`f: fn(int64, int64) -> int64`), the loader no longer splits them
    at the inner comma, and a fn pointer whose int/float class differs is a type mismatch (tests/diag_test.sh).
12. DONE closures: `fn(int x) -> int { ... }`, capture by value, stack or arena storage by a simple
    escape check (tests/stdlib/closures.hy). Deviation from the plan: the env travels in a runtime
    slot (hylian_clo_set/get in mem.hy), not r10, and a typed fn is one tagged word, not a pair;
    r10 is in the register allocator's pool, so using it means touching hygen. Heap closures leak.
13. DONE bounds on generics: `T: Ord` / Eq / Num / Integer / a class name, checked when an instance is
    made (compiler/mono.c; tests/stdlib/generic_bounds.hy, tests/diag_test.sh).

OPTIMIZATION
14. Cross-module inlining of runtime.hy/array.hy/mem.hy (separate objects). LOOKED AT, NOT DONE: no
    benchmark's hot loop calls into them (objdump: only hylian_int_to_str/println, once), so it cannot move
    bench/run.py; worth doing only for code that calls array/string helpers in a loop.
15. DONE induction-variable strength reduction (hyopt.c strength_reduce: t = i*K with i += c becomes a
    second counter). Correct (opt_test + fuzz pass) but matmul stays 0.0165s: the imul was not the
    bottleneck, the two bounds checks per iteration are. Next: hoist/version those checks out of the loop.
16. PARTLY DONE shrink-wrapping for the early-return shape (hyopt.c shrink_wrap_prep + lower_x64.c wrap_at): fib's
    `n < 2` path is now cmp/mov/ret with no pushes. Live-range splitting is still not done.
17. (bench this session, C/C++/Go only, rust not installed)
    fib 0.006 vs c 0.004 go 0.010 | loop tie | sieve tie | mandel 0.025 tie | collatz 0.093 (1st; c 0.108) |
    matmul 0.011 vs c 0.009 go 0.012. What got us there: x/2^k in the x%2^k==0 arm is a plain sar
    (div_exact_arm), 3*x+imm is one lea, fixed-size arrays have a known length (known_arr_len) and interval
    analysis over counted loops removes their bounds checks (range_bce), a[i*n+k] is split into a hoisted
    base + the induction variable (split_index), float expressions are CSE'd across blocks, and
    `if/while/for (a && b || c)` branch directly instead of materialising a bool (lower_jump_if; this exposed
    an if_convert bug with a label jumped to from two places, fixed). Still open: fib at 1.5x C (gcc turns
    the second recursive call into a loop with an accumulator), inner-loop unrolling for matmul.
    HYLIAN_DUMP_MIR=1 prints the optimised MIR; HYLIAN_OPT_OFF=shrinkwrap,bce,splitidx,div turn the new passes off.

